menu "Aliro serial console"

config ALIRO_CONSOLE_ENABLE
    bool "Interactive serial console"
    default y
    help
        The `aliro>` REPL on the serial port: status, identity, wifi,
        unlock, factory-reset.

        Turn this off for a build that runs the Matter stack. Starting the
        REPL installs the driver-based UART VFS, after which every ESP_LOG
        from every task goes through the UART driver and takes a mutex. With
        chip, NimBLE and Wi-Fi all logging concurrently, that path asserts
        inside a blocking semaphore take -- and since the panic handler logs
        too, it re-enters and recurses until the stack is gone.

        Everything the console does is also in the web UI, including the log
        view, so this costs a convenience rather than a capability.

endmenu
